hadiths[29]{hadithnumber,text}:
"133","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, he said: When the verse 'Pilgrimage to the House is a duty to Allah upon people who can find a way to it' was revealed, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the way? He said: Provision and a mount."
"134","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard an old man narrating to Abu Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wish to renew in the hearts of the believers: any child whose family performs Hajj with him and then he dies, it suffices for him; if he grows up, Hajj is obligatory upon him. And any slave whose family performs Hajj with him and then he dies, it suffices for him; if he is freed, Hajj is obligatory upon him."
"135","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed al-Tan'im as the miqat for the people of Makkah. Abu Dawud said: Sufyan said: This hadith is not known. Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razi narrated to us, Mihran narrated to us, he said: Sufyan said: This is hardly known, meaning the hadith of al-Tan'im."
"136","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram may kill the wolf ... and he mentioned the hadith."
"137","Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ziyad informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, he said: It reached me from 'A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning ostrich eggs: for each egg, fasting one day or feeding a poor person. Abu Dawud said: This hadith was given a connected chain, and this is the correct one."
"138","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, Matar al-Warraq narrated to us, that Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah told them from a man of the Ansar that a man in ihram trampled an ostrich nest with his mount. The man went to 'Ali and asked him about that. 'Ali said to him: For each egg, the striking of a she-camel or a camel fetus. The man went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him what 'Ali had said. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Ali has said what you heard, but come to the concession: upon you for each egg is fasting one day."
"139","Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah - meaning Ibn Sallam - narrated to us, from Yahya, Yazid ibn Nu'aym or Zayd ibn Nu'aym - Abu Tawbah doubted - informed me, that a man from Judham had intercourse with his wife while both were in ihram. The man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to them both: Complete your rites and offer a sacrifice, then return until, when you are at the place where you did what you did, separate so that neither of you sees the other. Upon you both is another Hajj; come forth until, when you are at the place where you did what you did, enter ihram, complete your rites, and offer a sacrifice."
"140","Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated on the night of the Ifadah on his mount, touching the Corner with his staff and kissing the staff."
"141","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened in all his 'Umrahs at the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and Abu Bakr hastened in the year of Hajj when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him, then Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, and the caliphs successively hastened likewise. Abu Dawud said: This hadith has been given a connected chain, but it is not authentic, and this is the correct one."
"142","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, he said: It is thought that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped on the night of Muzdalifah at the present stations of the imams. Ibn Bakr said: I think."
"143","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Zabban ibn Salman narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped on the day of 'Arafah by the rock facing the stations of the rulers at 'Arafah in the low land of the mountain, screening its people with a garment over him."
"144","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Makkah, prayed with one adhan and one iqamah, prayed at Mina with one iqamah, prayed at 'Arafah with two iqamahs, at Muzdalifah with two iqamahs, and prayed at al-Abtah in the valley on the day of departure the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha'."
"145","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, that Yahya, Rawh, and Ibn Bakr told them the meaning, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: 'Ata' said: It reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the adhan in the evening - meaning the evening of 'Arafah - and the iqamah on the night of Muzdalifah. Abu Dawud said: Yahya said: An iqamah, an iqamah. Abu Dawud said: This was given a connected chain, but it is not authentic."
"146","Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Hannad narrated to us, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two prayers at 'Arafah with an adhan and an iqamah."
"147","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, 'Umar - meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Wahid - narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Sulayman ibn Musa, he said: It is not preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he raised his hands with full raising except in three places: asking for rain, asking for victory, and the evening of 'Arafah; thereafter there was a lesser raising."
"148","Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, 'Awwam informed us, from al-Saffah ibn Matar, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of 'Arafah is the day on which people stand at 'Arafah."
"149","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn 'Allaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Ubaydah, he said: In the year in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, the people performed Hajj without an imam."
"150","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the day of 'Arafah and said: This is the day of the Greater Hajj. Those before you among the people of idols and ignorance would depart when the sun was seen upon the mountains as though it were the turbans of men, and would push forth from Muzdalifah when it shone upon the mountains as though they were the turbans of men. Our guidance differs from the guidance of the people of polytheism and idols."
"151","Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Tawus said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped to the left of the imam's prayer place at Mina. Others of our shaykhs besides Tawus said like the saying of Tawus, adding: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives to camp beside the house - his house at Mina - commanded the Ansar to camp in the ravine behind the house, and said to the people: Camp, pointing to the areas of Mina."
"152","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Ata' informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to permit the sacrificial camel, when its owner needed it, to be loaded and ridden without exhaustion. I said: What? He said: For the walking man, the one following on the way, and if it gives birth, its calf and its equivalent are carried upon it."
"153","'Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, that Sulayman ibn Hayyan told them from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata' al-Khurasani, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A sacrificial camel is due upon me, I can afford it but cannot find one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughter seven sheep."
"154","Al-Walid ibn 'Utbah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, with its chain and meaning."
"155","Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to me, from Yahya, from 'Ikrimah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed his garments at al-Tan'im."
"156","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi - a Kufan - narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash, Sa'id ibn Yusuf narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from 'Ikrimah the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed his garments at al-Tan'im while in ihram."
"157","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Waki', from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man in ihram girded with a shiny rope and said: O owner of the rope, cast it off."
"158","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, al-Walid informed us, from 'Ali - meaning Ibn Hawshab - I heard Makhul say: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment saturated with safflower dye and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to perform Hajj; may I enter ihram in this? He said: Do you have another? She said: No. He said: Then enter ihram in it."
"159","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Bakr - meaning Ibn Mudar - narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Ghazziyyah, from Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stoned the farthest Jamrah, returned to the slaughter place, sacrificed, shaved, then hastened to the Tawaf immediately."
"160","Ibn Khallad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the Tawaf every night of the nights of Mina. Abu Dawud said: This has been given a connected chain."
"161","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, and Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, that Jarir told them, from Mansur, from Ibrahim: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept on the night of departure at al-Abtah a sleep, then set out before dawn. Qutaybah did not mention the night of departure."
